   1362  fc3e							; $FD80` at $FE48). IN: A = kill clock (EnemyRamP-1), Y = MetaB b6 hot bit
   1363  fc3e							; ($40/0 — staged bank2-side; MetaB lives in bank2 models_data ROM, a
   1364  fc3e							; (RoomPF0Lo),Y fetch here would see bank3's pad). OUT (2026-10-14b):
   1365  fc3e							; C=0 passable (A ignored) / C=1 + A≠0 kill / C=1 + A=0 SOLID block —
   1366  fc3e							; returned through the $FBEE pad (sta $1FF8 executed here, rts fetched
   1367  fc3e							; from bank2's byte-identical copy) to OvShutBand's jsr — A and C
   1368  fc3e							; survive both; X/Y clobbered (OvShutBand reloads A before the latch).
   1369  fc3e							; Kill semantics (user spec 2026-10-14, superseded the 2026-10-13
   1370  fc3e							; endpoint-only rule): a horizontal containment gate (after the clock
   1371  fc3e							; math, before the hot/cold split) — the player's lit span must sit
   1372  fc3e							; inside the column [BallX-7, BallX] or the call returns passable
   1373  fc3e							; (side brush, user bug 2026-10-14: touching the closed block from the
   1374  fc3e							; side is not a crunch). Then hot band (MetaB b6) = touching ANY
   1375  fc3e							; closed slice kills (endpoint test ≡ any-part: the ping-pong states
   1376  fc3e							; $11/$1B/$1F never have a closed middle with open ends). Cold band =
   1377  fc3e							; containment only: kill iff the whole sprite sits inside CLOSED
   1378  fc3e							; slices (crunched) — $1F trivially; $1B/$11 iff the box misses the
   1379  fc3e							; aperture (H≥gapHi or F<gapLo). Touching an edge from the open side
   1380  fc3e							; is not a cold kill — that is what the hot flag is for. Every
   1381  fc3e							; NON-kill outcome (side brush, opening half, totally closed, the
   1382  fc3e							; aperture at the player's Y) goes through the solidity test
   1383  fc3e							; (.V3solidBody): both endpoints open → passable, else SOLID block —
   1384  fc3e							; the punched cell must not be walkable through a closed shutter
   1385  fc3e							; (user 2026-10-14b).
   1386  fc3e							; Clock parity: RefreshEnemyY inc'd EnemyRamP at overscan entry, so
   1387  fc3e							; clock-1 = the exact value the kernel rendered slices from this frame.
   1388  fc3e							; Endpoints: RoomY (head) + RoomY+11 (feet = PLAYER_SPRITE_H-1) — every
   1389  fc3e							; open state's gap is >=13 lines ($1B = the 13-line center slice), so
   1390  fc3e							; both endpoints open ⟺ the whole sprite is clear of that state.
   1391  fc3e							; Ping-pong constants (#32/#4) = bank2 VcrCoveredState + CrunchClock
   1392  fc3e							; (verify_build check_crunch_clock asserts the trio).
